@Ally
are you sure both the vlue's script and the add-on are active? Then I would ask the same questions
@Kes
asked.

@Ally
the command is there but it won't work (my script ignores it), I just forgot to delete it. The only way to get it working would be to add Vlue's script and activate the add-on (it's not active by default, one would need to read the instructions on the add-on to activate it).
But the add-on was designed just to make my script compatible with Vlue's. If you don't want to use the time system, there's no point in activating it.

@Espilonarge
I use both Effectus and this script without a crash, so I think it might be something specific to your setup.
After installing these, did you start a New Game?  Trying to load an existing save file probably won't work.

@Espilonarge
What happens if you don't have the map set to scroll?
Also, what is the comment "event size: 32, 32" referring to?  It isn't one I'm using in Ace with that script, so I don't know what it's pointing to.

@Espilonarge
unfortunately Effectus is closed source and I can't access it to further study the problem. But by doing a quick search, I learned that it's a heavy modification script, thus it is likely that it will break other scripts.
If you open my script and search for adjust_x or adjust_y, you will see that I don't touch this method, that is, it's not being overwritten or aliased. So I think one of the following variables is not initialized when I call the adjust methods in my script:
@ms_effectus_dref_display_x
@ms_effectus_adjx
@ms_effectus_dref_display_y
@ms_effectus_adjy
I'm sorry, but I can't do much about this
